Arguments addressed by revisionist :
2. Assailing the impugned order, revisionist submitted that the impugned order passed by the Ld.Trial Court is bad in law and has been passed in haste without considering the submissions of the petitioners; the petitioners have been falsely implicated and there was never any act of dowry demands made by the petitioners;
the marriage between the complainant namely Huma @ Uma Prazapati and accused no.1 Vinod Kumar is a love marriage and the petitioners have no role in the said marriage; that the petitioners have never lived/met/talked/contacted (through physically or telephonically) and even never seen the complainant after her marriage with the accused no.1; that both complainant and accused no.1 in collusion lodged the present FIR against the petitioners which is pending before the Ld. Trial Court only to harass the old aged petitioners and to black mail Criminal Revision No. 321/2022 them for their properties; that the accused nos. 2, 5 & 6 have already been discharged by the Ld. Trial Court by saying that "no grave suspicion arises to charge accused Mahesh, Manju and Prabha" and that the petitioners are old aged persons and are suffering from various old aged health issues.
